# acme_normal.wsp13 — F3, STAGE 1, spec acme_normal-wsp-v13
# Author of the numbers: claude-fable-5-2 (Anthropic), docs/wsp/research/phys_sflame_f3.md (E4). DATA-INFORMED.
# Transcribed by an engineer (claude-opus-5-5) without choosing any number.
# Stage 1 of the owner's three: the parts that concern the flames F2 already answers. The burner limit is an
# input of the test (condition burner_limit_c); the heating law has its flame-temperature factor and the
# stream-conductivity power; the methane row step with the weak-flame shift column; the ethylene dilution term
# of the growth members. Left out (stage 2 and 3): the helium row of the diluent table, the hydrogen row and
# the blends; those inputs are refused, as in F2. The slot law values are F2's, copied statement by statement
# by tools/wsp/committee4_edits.py; the fuel and diluent tables are configs/models/acme/fuel_tables/
# normal-f3s1-*.wsp.
#
# The committee lines of F2, unchanged:
